cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tamias in academic work, please cite the architecture specification."
title: "Tamias: Transition-Aware Inference Economics for Coding Agents"
abstract: >-
  Tamias is an observation instrument for inference economics. It records
  per-request token metadata in a canonical SQLite ledger without persisting
  prompt text, source code, tool arguments or assistant text. Observed cost,
  estimated exposure and causal effect are kept as separate quantities, and
  any value that cannot be established from a source is recorded as UNKNOWN
  rather than guessed.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "UNPUBLISHED"
keywords:
  - inference
  - economics
  - coding agents
  - cost observability
  - reproducibility
notes: >-
  Version 0.1.0 implements the observation path only (scan and the canonical
  ledger). Reporting, receipts, attribution and causal modules are stubs.